j.allen.henderson@gmail.com wrote:

> I killed a bugbear on top of an "unfresh" bugbear body, and the two
> stacked, right next to an altar.  I picked up one, tried to offer it
> (nothing happened), dropped it elsewhere, and tried the other one.
> Nothing happened again, when one definitely should have been fresh
> enough to work.
> 
> Has this "bug" been addressed before?

It's not a bug. When corpses stack, their ages are averaged. The game
doesn't keep track of which corpse in a stack is the fresher one (if it
did, they wouldn't stack).

This can also work in your favour (the fresh corpse makes the old one fit
to sacrifice) but apparently in this case the older corpse was *much* too
old.

   Raisse, poisoned by a rotted kobold corpse

